NOTE: Download LB Wifi OFF Software: https://fileoss.lbtool.net/webfile/lbtool-tool/LB-WIFI-OFF-1.0.0.zip

== Problem description ==
On MacBook models with M-series chipset (M1/M2/M3/M4), Wi-Fi can stop working due to a failed Wi-Fi IC. Even after macOS reinstall, the machine may show “Exclamation Mark on Wifi Toggle” because the Wi-Fi IC is paired to the logic board via ECID binding. Replacing the IC requires unbinding and rebinding the Wi-Fi chip to the MacBook.
== Symptoms ==

* Wi-Fi greyed out in macOS.
* "Exclamation mark" on WiFi
* Bluetooth may also fail in some cases.
* macOS reinstall, PRAM/SMC reset do not fix the issue.<br />[[File:Mac-wifi-bad.png|center|thumb|WiFi Not Working (Figure 1) ]]

=== Diagnostic Steps ===

# Boot macOS → check if Wi-Fi toggle is unavailable.
# Enter System Information > Wi-Fi → confirm hardware not detected.
# Ensure issue is not antenna or connector related (inspect for corrosion/damage).
# Verify power rails to Wi-Fi IC are present. If power is correct but IC is still not enumerating, proceed with replacement & rebinding.<br />
=== Repair Steps ===

==== Software Setup ====

# Install [https://fileoss.lbtool.net/webfile/lbtool-tool/LB-WIFI-OFF-1.0.0.zip Luban software]  (LB-WIFI-OFF) using a pendrive.
# Launch Luban software with internet connection (mobile hotspot works).
# The software will unbind Wi-Fi and read the MacBook ECID automatically.[[File:Mac-wifi-unbind-successful.png|center|thumb|Successful WiFi Unbind]]
# Verify in “About This Mac” that serial number is correct.[[File:Mac-wifi-unbind-sn-match.png|center|thumb|Verify Serial No. is same after unbind.]]
# Shut down MacBook.

==== Board Work ====
6. Disconnect battery, remove logic board from chassis.

7. Remove Wi-Fi IC with hot air.
[[File:Mac-wifi-removal.png|center|thumb|Remove MacBook WiFi IC]]
8. Clean solder pads using wick + flux until smooth.

==== Programming the Wi-Fi IC ====
9. Connect Luban programmer with Wi-Fi IC reading module.

10. Place Wi-Fi IC in the module.
[[File:Mac-wifi-programmer-install.png|center|thumb|WiFi IC in LB Tool]]
11. Open Luban tool → wait for IC to be read.
[[File:Lbtool-wifi-reading.png|center|thumb|New LB WiFi IC reading]]
12. Input the MacBook serial number (recorded earlier).

13. Click Check Now.
[[File:Mac-wifi-serial-input.png|center|thumb|Input Serial Number]]
14. After verifying, Click Write Server Data.
[[File:Write-server-data.png|center|thumb|Write Server Data]]
15. Verify if written info (Serial) is correct.

16. Confirm write.
[[File:Verify-serial.png|center|thumb|Verify Serial Number]]
17. Wait for successful confirmation.

==== Reinstallation ====
18. Reball Wi-Fi IC with correct stencil.

19. Install IC back onto the logic board.

20. Clean with IPA, inspect under microscope.

21. Reassemble MacBook, reconnect battery.

==== Verification ====

* Boot into macOS.
* Wi-Fi should now be detected and toggle enabled.
* System Information should show Wi-Fi hardware with correct addresses.
* Connect to a Wi-Fi network and run stress test (download/upload).[[File:Wifi-fixed-successfully.png|center|thumb|WiFi fixed successfully.]]